keys:

    ctrl+t (or ctrl+n)      new shell tab
    ctrl+w                  close tab
    ctrl+→/← (or ctrl+f/b)  next / previous tab


install to `~/.local/bin/tabs`:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/install.sh | bash


update with:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/update.sh | bash


make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your path, then run `tabs`.
to use `tabs` when you type `tmux`, add `alias tmux=tabs` to your shell config.
`command tmux` still runs the real tmux.


shared global agent rules (optional):

    tabs sync-rules --dry-run
    tabs sync-rules

create your own nonempty policy at ~/.config/agents/AGENTS.md first
(or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agents/AGENTS.md). You can pass a different file:

    tabs sync-rules --dry-run ~/dotfiles/agents/shared.md
    tabs sync-rules ~/dotfiles/agents/shared.md

the command copies this policy into a marked section of:

    ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md       ($CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/CLAUDE.md if set)
    ~/.codex/AGENTS.md        ($CODEX_HOME/AGENTS.md if set)
    ~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md     ($PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR/AGENTS.md if set)

instructions outside the section are preserved. Existing files get a
one-time .before-tabs-rules backup; unchanged files are not rewritten.
Symlink destinations and malformed/duplicate managed sections are refused.
All destinations are validated before any instruction file is changed.
Dry runs print diffs without creating destination directories or backups.

if your files already contain BEGIN/END USER GIT APPROVAL RULES markers,
explicitly migrate that old section instead of keeping contradictory rules:

    tabs sync-rules --dry-run --migrate-git-rules
    tabs sync-rules --migrate-git-rules

review your policy and the dry-run diff before applying. For example, a
single-confirmation policy could say:

    Ask once before a clearly scoped commit-and-push workflow, naming the
    changes, remote and branch. Approval covers local preparation and retries
    of the same operation. Ask again if changes or destination change, or if
    force-pushing or remote deletion becomes necessary. Do not treat approval
    as authorization for unrelated GitHub writes.

tabs ships no mandatory policy. Installation/update never syncs rules,
and this command does not modify native tool permissions or sandbox settings.
Edit the source and rerun sync-rules to propagate changes. Restart agents
so they load the updated instructions; the rules also apply outside tabs.

run the isolated tests with: bash tests/shared-rules.sh
